  "id": "Camden-2026_1073_P",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Replacement of 3 x existing air conditioning units with 4 x units (retrospective).",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The air conditioning units, due to their number, size, and prominent siting, create visual clutter that harm the character and appearance of the host building, the wider street scene, and the setting of the Rochester Conservation Area contrary to policies D1 (Design) and D2 (Heritage) of the Camden Local Plan (2017).",
    "Reason : 2 - The development results in unacceptable noise and disturbance to neighbouring residential occupiers, as the air conditioning units exceed the Council's adopted noise thresholds and the proposal fails to include the necessary acoustic mitigation, contrary to Policies A1 and A4 of the Camden Local Plan 2017."
  ],
